WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.529
Every model makes

00:00:01.341 --> 00:00:02.154
a hidden bet

00:00:01.966 --> 00:00:03.050
about uncertainty

00:00:03.582 --> 00:00:04.666
Christian Henning's

00:00:04.478 --> 00:00:05.598
guide argues that

00:00:05.504 --> 00:00:06.648
every model makes

00:00:06.459 --> 00:00:07.438
an assumption about

00:00:07.249 --> 00:00:08.086
uncertainty

00:00:08.275 --> 00:00:09.419
often without saying

00:00:09.231 --> 00:00:09.773
so

00:00:09.867 --> 00:00:10.952
and where data

00:00:10.764 --> 00:00:11.447
is rare

00:00:11.542 --> 00:00:12.886
that assumption decides

00:00:12.698 --> 00:00:13.464
the answer

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:14.768
Take a coin

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:15.145
flip

00:00:15.284 --> 00:00:15.897
If we do

00:00:15.709 --> 00:00:16.522
not measure how

00:00:16.334 --> 00:00:17.006
the coin is

00:00:16.817 --> 00:00:17.407
thrown

00:00:17.572 --> 00:00:18.232
the best we

00:00:18.044 --> 00:00:18.975
can say is

00:00:18.787 --> 00:00:19.895
fifty fifty

00:00:19.978 --> 00:00:21.286
and that uncertainty

00:00:21.098 --> 00:00:22.312
is aleatoric

00:00:22.838 --> 00:00:23.687
The post then

00:00:23.498 --> 00:00:25.396
covers epistemic uncertainty

00:00:25.432 --> 00:00:26.340
calibration

00:00:26.529 --> 00:00:27.649
Bayesian inference

00:00:27.461 --> 00:00:29.158
and conformal guarantees

00:00:29.277 --> 00:00:29.913
and how to

00:00:29.725 --> 00:00:31.080
judge when uncertainty

00:00:30.892 --> 00:00:31.977
must be faithful

00:00:31.788 --> 00:00:32.708
to be useful

00:00:33.246 --> 00:00:34.260
Full story on

00:00:34.071 --> 00:00:34.967
the dashboard
